# style_only_blank.xlsx -- FROZEN EXPECTATION.
# A reading of the openpyxl-authored fixture against plan 01 D2/D3/D4.
# Corrected ONLY when that reading was wrong -- never edited to chase an FSA1 regression.
#
# B1 states a solid FF00B0F0 fill and no value. A visually non-null style IS occupancy, so the
# block spans A1:B1 and the grid line carries two fields, the second empty. One row is the whole
# block, so the fill is a COLUMN rule; column 2 of 2 is `td:last-child`.
file: Blank/@presentation.css
|@scope (A1:B1) {
|  td:last-child { background-color: #00b0f0 }
|}
